HTML Attribute Interview Q&A

1. What are HTML attributes? → Extra info for elements, written in name-value pairs.
2. Difference between id and class? → id = unique, class = reusable.
3. title attribute? → Shows tooltip on hover.
4. alt attribute? → Alternative text for images, aids accessibility.
5. href attribute? → Defines link destination.
6. src vs href? → src = embedded resource, href = hyperlink.
7. style attribute? → Inline CSS styling.
8. lang attribute? → Declares language of document.
9. tabindex attribute? → Controls keyboard navigation order.
10. disabled attribute? → Makes form element inactive.
11. readonly attribute? → Field uneditable but submitted.
12. disabled vs readonly? → Disabled not submitted, readonly submitted.
13. placeholder attribute? → Hint text in input fields.
14. required attribute? → Field must be filled before submit.
15. maxlength attribute? → Limits input length.
16. value attribute? → Sets initial value of input.
17. checked attribute? → Preselects checkbox/radio.
18. selected attribute? → Preselects dropdown option.
19. download attribute? → Forces file download from link.
20. target attribute? → Defines where link opens (_blank, _self).
21. rel attribute? → Relationship between current doc and linked doc.
22. type attribute (input)? → Defines input type (text, email, etc.).
23. name attribute? → Identifies form field for submission.
24. for attribute (label)? → Associates label with input.
25. data-* attribute? → Custom data storage for JS.
26. draggable attribute? → Makes element draggable.
27. spellcheck attribute? → Enables/disables spell checking.
28. hidden attribute? → Hides element from page.
29. contenteditable attribute? → Makes element editable in browser.
30. autofocus attribute? → Auto-focuses input on page load.
